title: "Complex Technologies and Economic Value"
collection: publications
category: working 
excerpt: "This paper proposes a measure for industry-level technological complexity using a novel Network Diversity Score, which captures the connections between fundamental knowledge components. This approach outperforms other complexity metrics in key tests. The findings show that technological complexity rose steadily at both technology sector and NAICS industry levels until the Covid-19 pandemic, after which labor-intensive industries experienced a sharp decline. It is also found that the drivers of technological complexity vary with industry concentration. In more competitive industries, greater investment intensity is strongly associated with subsequent technological complexity, whereas this relationship is substantially weaker in more concentrated markets. The economic impact analysis further shows that technological complexity primarily benefits the labor market rather than firms. Greater technological complexity is associated with hiring more lower-paid workers but not with firms' higher subsequent profitability and market valuation."
